# 8. Severity Classification

All agents must use the same severity model.

| Severity | Description |
|---|---|
| CRITICAL | Severe defect, security exposure, application instability, or major architectural violation with significant consequences. |
| HIGH | Important defect with meaningful impact on correctness, security, performance, or maintainability. |
| MEDIUM | Maintainability, reliability, or quality issue that should be corrected. |
| LOW | Minor improvement or low-impact convention violation. |
| INFO | Positive observation or informational recommendation, not a defect. |

## 8.1 Severity rules

- Severity must reflect actual impact.
- Do not classify theoretical optimizations as HIGH.
- Do not classify style preferences as CRITICAL.
- Use confidence separately from severity.
- A finding with insufficient evidence must not be presented as confirmed.
- When appropriate, request profiling or runtime validation.

