# 9. Deduplication Strategy

Different agents may identify the same underlying problem.

For example:

- Kotlin Agent detects incorrect coroutine scope ownership.
- Memory Agent detects a coroutine retaining an Activity.
- Performance Agent detects unnecessary background work.

These findings may share a root cause but represent different technical impacts.

The aggregator must distinguish between:

1. Exact duplicates.
2. Related findings.
3. Independent findings in the same file.
4. Different symptoms caused by the same root cause.

## 9.1 Deduplication rules

Merge findings only when they represent the same underlying violation and substantially overlap in evidence.

Preserve all relevant skill and agent references.

Do not merge independent issues merely because they occur in the same method.

## 9.2 Consolidated finding example

```json
{
  "id": "AUDIT-001",
  "severity": "HIGH",
  "confidence": "HIGH",
  "file": "feature/home/presentation/HomeViewModel.kt",
  "line_start": 32,
  "line_end": 40,
  "title": "Incorrect coroutine lifecycle ownership",
  "agents": [
    "android-kotlin-agent",
    "android-memory-agent"
  ],
  "skills": [
    "android-coroutines-flow-audit",
    "android-memory-leak-audit"
  ],
  "root_cause": "Coroutine launched in an inappropriate scope",
  "recommendation": "Use a lifecycle-appropriate coroutine scope and ensure cancellation."
}
```

The consolidated finding must preserve references to the original agent reports.

