# 13. Gerrit Integration

Gerrit integration is a future extension of the architecture.

The system should be able to analyze a specific Gerrit change and optionally publish selected findings as review comments.

## 13.1 Proposed workflow

```mermaid
flowchart TD
    A["Gerrit Change"] --> B["Fetch Change Metadata"]
    B --> C["Get Patchset Diff"]
    C --> D["Changed Files Audit"]
    D --> E["Execute Specialized Agents"]
    E --> F["Aggregate Findings"]
    F --> G["Review Comment Filter"]
    G --> H["Severity Threshold"]
    H --> I["Publish Gerrit Comments"]
    F --> J["Generate Audit Reports"]
```

## 13.2 Gerrit requirements

- Identify project, change number, and patchset.
- Retrieve the correct patchset diff.
- Analyze modified lines and surrounding context.
- Associate findings with valid file paths and line numbers.
- Publish only findings meeting the configured severity threshold.
- Avoid duplicate comments.
- Preserve report references.
- Support dry-run mode.
- Never publish comments without validating that the referenced line belongs to the target patchset.

## 13.3 Suggested CLI

```bash
android-audit \
  --gerrit-change 123456 \
  --patchset 3 \
  --severity high \
  --dry-run
```

This command is a proposed interface; the Gerrit adapter must be implemented separately.

