# 15. Implementation Phases

Implementation should be incremental.

## Phase 1 — Foundation

Deliverables:

- Repository structure.
- Orchestrator definition.
- Eight agent definitions.
- Reuse of existing skills.
- Shared report contract.
- Severity configuration.

Acceptance criteria:

- All agents can be discovered.
- Every agent has defined responsibilities.
- Skills are assigned correctly.
- Reports follow the common contract.

## Phase 2 — Individual Audits

Deliverables:

- Architecture Agent.
- Kotlin Agent.
- Compose Agent.
- Performance Agent.
- Memory Agent.
- Testing Agent.
- Security Agent.
- Build Agent.

Acceptance criteria:

- Each agent can independently analyze its domain.
- Findings include exact file and line references.
- Findings include evidence and recommendations.
- Agents do not modify source code.

## Phase 3 — Orchestration

Deliverables:

- Agent dispatcher.
- Parallel execution support.
- Execution status tracking.
- Failure handling.
- Result collection.

Acceptance criteria:

- The orchestrator can execute multiple agents.
- Agent failures do not silently disappear.
- Incomplete audits are explicitly identified.

## Phase 4 — Report Aggregation

Deliverables:

- Finding validation.
- Deduplication.
- Severity prioritization.
- Individual reports.
- Executive report.
- JSON export.

Acceptance criteria:

- Every agent produces an individual report.
- The executive report consolidates all results.
- Duplicate findings retain original references.
- Reports contain no invented information.

## Phase 5 — CLI

Deliverables:

- `--full`.
- `--changed-only`.
- `--agent`.
- `--agents`.
- `--module`.
- Report format selection.

Acceptance criteria:

- Commands validate inputs.
- Git scope is correctly identified.
- Exit codes reflect execution status.

## Phase 6 — Gerrit Integration

Deliverables:

- Gerrit change retrieval.
- Patchset analysis.
- Finding-to-diff mapping.
- Review comment filtering.
- Dry-run mode.
- Optional comment publishing.

Acceptance criteria:

- Comments reference valid changed lines.
- Only configured severities are published.
- Duplicate comments are avoided.
- No comments are published in dry-run mode.

