# 17. Success Criteria

The system is considered ready when:

1. Eight specialized agents are available.
2. Existing skills are reused instead of duplicated.
3. Every agent has a clearly defined technical responsibility.
4. Full project audits work.
5. Changed-file audits work.
6. Individual reports are generated.
7. A consolidated report is generated.
8. Findings contain verifiable evidence.
9. Duplicate findings are handled correctly.
10. Failed or skipped agents are visible in the report.
11. The audit does not modify application source code.
12. The architecture supports future Gerrit integration.

---

# 18. Final Architecture Principles

The project must follow these principles:

- One orchestrator, multiple specialized agents.
- One technical responsibility per agent.
- Skills are reusable knowledge, not agents.
- Agents must not duplicate specialized rules.
- Findings must be evidence-based.
- Reports must be independently auditable.
- Deduplication must preserve technical context.
- Parallel execution must not compromise result quality.
- Source code must remain unchanged during auditing.
- Gerrit integration must remain a separate adapter.

